{
  "tool_id": "art-497-validator-change-control-receipt",
  "note": "golden_hash filled by golden-parity.test.mjs --update. Vector 1 is a clean weight_change with quorum met. Vector 2 is an add with quorum short (SHORT is not itself an exception -- it is a policy outcome, distinct from a structural exception). Vector 3 is a remove with multiple simultaneous exceptions (nonzero posterior weight, no authorizer, unstated quorum policy, missing epoch, zero total stake). Vector 4 is the empty-input finite-gate case: every field resolves to an explicit null/0/false, never NaN or undefined. Vectors 12 to 27 are the weight-statedness cure corpus: weights, total stake and quorum numbers are statements only as finite JSON numbers or as one strict decimal-string form (the page port sends DOM input strings, pinned by the accept-strict-numeric-string-form positive control), empty strings, booleans, arrays and junk refuse NOT_STATED, negatives refuse NEGATIVE, nothing is coerced or clamped, and non-string as_of, effective_epoch and validator_ref are missing statements.",
